#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351078 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e5256297-c928-54e3-bf4d-35f5734f5632" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing Surface Integrals Over Parametric Surfaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4518e3d7-a24f-5ca6-a02e-940fc55f5343" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({u}^{2}-{v}^{2}-2u)\\sqrt{8}v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351080} {:answer/id #uuid "e2069f29-4d51-5f60-a9dd-fafb3f575ee1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({u}^{2}-{v}^{2})\\sqrt{8}u" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351081} {:answer/id #uuid "33a00a0e-ab3b-5331-9800-ea0eae6e2581" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({u}^{2}+{v}^{2}+u)\\sqrt{8v}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351082} {:answer/id #uuid "16a98401-3809-5ca7-b405-9897bc9b31cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({v}^{2}-{u}^{2}-2)\\sqrt{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351083} {:answer/id #uuid "55a55a49-a53d-5f4f-8006-c92711673a33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({u}^{2}+2v+2u)\\sqrt{8}v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351084}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4518e3d7-a24f-5ca6-a02e-940fc55f5343" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({u}^{2}-{v}^{2}-2u)\\sqrt{8}v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351080} :answer-field/id #uuid "b2809c52-243d-56a4-937d-e75412acf949" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351079}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "60828e8e-d700-5ec8-b0aa-d96b2e205b74" :question/math-academy-id "q-161286" :question/problem "$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nConsider the surface integral of the function \n$f(x,y,z)=-x-y-z$ \nover the parametric surface \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,{v}^{2}-{u}^{2},\\,u⟩\n$$\n\nfor $(u,v)\\in D⊆{R}^{2}.$ What is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({v}^{2}-{u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-2u,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({v}^{2}-{u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2v,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -2u & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2v & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}-2u & 1 \\\\ 2v & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2u \\\\ 0 & 2v\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2u,\\,0,\\,2v⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨-2v,\\,0,\\,2v⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-2v)^{2}+(0)^{2}+(2v)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{v}^{2}+4{v}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{8}v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(u,v)) & =(-x-y-z)\\,{|}_{x=u\\,y={v}^{2}-{u}^{2}\\,z=u} \\\\  & =-u-({v}^{2}-{u}^{2})-u \\\\  & ={u}^{2}-{v}^{2}-2u\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,({u}^{2}-{v}^{2}-2u)\\sqrt{8}v\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
